# Design System Audit Tool (Dev Only)

The DS highlighter (`DesignSystemAudit`, the **dev menu**, the **DS identifier** switch, `data-ds-component` markers, and `dsMarker`) is a **local testing tool**. It is not a product feature.

## Never Ship To Production

On any **commit**, **push**, or **deploy** (including Vercel production):

- Do not treat this tool as something that should appear on the live site
- Do not remove, weaken, or bypass the `process.env.NODE_ENV === "development"` gates
- Do not mount `DesignSystemAudit` unconditionally in `portfolio-main/app/layout.tsx` or any other layout/page
- Do not add production-facing UI, routes, or feature flags that turn the highlighter on for visitors
- Do not copy the overlay, toggle, or highlight styles into shared production components

## Required Gates

These must stay in place:

| Surface | Required gate |
| --- | --- |
| Overlay mount | [`portfolio-main/app/layout.tsx`](portfolio-main/app/layout.tsx) renders `<DesignSystemAudit />` only when `process.env.NODE_ENV === "development"` |
| Component markers | [`portfolio-main/lib/ds-marker.ts`](portfolio-main/lib/ds-marker.ts) returns `{}` unless `NODE_ENV` is `"development"` |
| Overlay UI | Lives under [`portfolio-main/components/dev/`](portfolio-main/components/dev/) and is imported only behind the layout gate |

Next production builds set `NODE_ENV` to `"production"`, so the overlay and `data-ds-component` attributes must compile out. If a change would make either appear in a production bundle or on the live site, stop and revert it.

## Marker Usage

When marking a shared design-system component for the audit tool, use `dsMarker("Name")` on the component root. Do not hard-code `data-ds-component` on pages, and do not add markers that skip the `dsMarker` development check.
